  "question": {
    "text": "The frequency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#957;</mi></mfenced></math> of an oscillating liquid drop may depend upon radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>r</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;of the drop, density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#961;</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;of liquid and the surface tension <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>s</mi></mfenced></math> of the liquid as:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><msup><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></math>.&nbsp;The values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> respectively are&nbsp;",
